## 1. Single-file prototype

Save as `index.html`. The API supplies “Thursday” but no calendar date; this prototype explicitly uses **Thursday, October 15, 2026** as a demo date. It does not create real bookings.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>PawPath — Harbor Street booking</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --primary: #7FD1AE;
    /* Accessibility override: brand white fails contrast on mint. */
    --primary-label: #1D2B33;
    --ink: #1D2B33;
    --surface: #FFFFFF;
    --muted: #5E6B73;
    --radius: 12px;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif;
  }
  main { max-width: 460px; padding: 20px 16px 32px; margin: auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 26px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 8px 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.3; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
  h3 { font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 10px; }
  p { margin: 8px 0 16px; }
  .brand { font-weight: 750; margin: 0; }
  .muted, small { color: var(--muted); }
  small { display: block; font-size: 14px; }
  .notice {
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .progress {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 20px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .progress li { border-top: 3px solid var(--muted); padding-top: 6px; }
  .progress [aria-current="step"] {
    border-color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 750;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  fieldset { min-width: 0; border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  legend { font-weight: 650; padding: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .options { display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .times { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .option {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 10px;
    min-height: 64px;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 2px solid var(--muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    cursor: pointer;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .option:has(input:checked) {
    border-color: var(--ink);
    background: #EDF9F3;
  }
  input[type="radio"] {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    flex: 0 0 20px;
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    accent-color: var(--ink);
  }
  .option strong { display: block; }
  :focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--ink);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .summary {
    margin-top: 24px;
    padding: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 8px 12px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  dt { color: var(--muted); }
  dd { margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 20px; }
  button {
    min-height: 48px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: white;
    color: var(--ink);
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 650;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .primary {
    flex: 1;
    background: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary-label);
  }
  button:disabled {
    background: #EEF1F2;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-color: var(--muted);
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .edits { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .edits button { font-size: 14px; }
  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px; height: 1px;
    padding: 0; margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <header>
    <p class="brand">PawPath</p>
    <h1>Harbor Street clinic</h1>
    <p class="notice">
      <strong>Interactive demo</strong><br>
      Thursday, October 15, 2026 is an illustrative date assigned to
      the supplied Thursday slots. All times are clinic-local.
      No real booking will be created.
    </p>
  </header>

  <ol class="progress" aria-label="Booking progress">
    <li>1 Service</li>
    <li>2 Vet</li>
    <li>3 Time</li>
    <li>4 Confirm</li>
  </ol>

  <form id="booking">
    <section id="screen" aria-labelledby="step-title"></section>

    <aside class="summary" aria-labelledby="summary-title">
      <h3 id="summary-title">Your appointment</h3>
      <dl>
        <dt>Service</dt><dd id="sum-service">Not selected</dd>
        <dt>Price</dt><dd id="sum-price">Not selected</dd>
        <dt>Vet</dt><dd id="sum-vet">Not selected</dd>
        <dt>Date</dt><dd>Thursday, October 15, 2026 (demo)</dd>
        <dt>Time</dt><dd id="sum-time">Not selected</dd>
        <dt>Clinic</dt>
        <dd>Harbor Street<br>12 Harbor Street, Example City</dd>
      </dl>
    </aside>

    <div class="actions" id="actions">
      <button type="button" id="back">Back</button>
      <button type="submit" class="primary" id="next">Continue</button>
    </div>
  </form>
  <p id="status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-atomic="true"></p>
</main>

<script>
const DEMO_DATE = "2026-10-15";
const DAY = new Date(DEMO_DATE + "T12:00:00Z").getUTCDay();

const services = {
  "Wellness exam": {
    minutes: 30, price: "$65", restricted: false
  },
  "Vaccination visit": {
    minutes: 15, price: "$40", restricted: false
  },
  "Dental cleaning": {
    minutes: 90, price: "from $280", restricted: true, estimate: true
  },
  "Exotic pet check-up": {
    minutes: 45, price: "$85", restricted: true
  }
};
const vets = {
  "Mary Major": [2, 4, 6],
  "Richard Miles": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
};
const rawSlots = [
  {"vet":"Richard Miles","service":"Exotic pet check-up","start":"10:00"},
  {"vet":"Mary Major","service":"Exotic pet check-up","start":"11:00"},
  {"vet":"Mary Major","service":"Dental cleaning","start":"11:30"},
  {"vet":"Richard Miles","service":"Wellness exam","start":"12:30"},
  {"vet":"Richard Miles","service":"Wellness exam","start":"14:00"},
  {"vet":"Mary Major","service":"Wellness exam","start":"16:45"}
];

const minutes = time => {
  if (!/^(?:[01]\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\d$/.test(time)) return NaN;
  const [h, m] = time.split(":").map(Number);
  return h * 60 + m;
};
const clock = n =>
  String(Math.floor(n / 60)).padStart(2, "0") + ":" +
  String(n % 60).padStart(2, "0");
const qualifies = (vet, service) =>
  Boolean(vets[vet] && services[service]) &&
  (!services[service].restricted || vet === "Mary Major");

function bookable(slot) {
  const service = services[slot.service];
  if (!service || slot.date !== DEMO_DATE ||
      !qualifies(slot.vet, slot.service) ||
      !vets[slot.vet].includes(DAY)) return false;

  const start = minutes(slot.start);
  const end = start + service.minutes;
  // The ENTIRE appointment must fit in one open interval.
  return [[540, 720], [780, 1020]].some(
    ([open, close]) => start >= open && end <= close
  );
}

// Date assignment is a demo fixture, not information from the API.
const slots = rawSlots
  .map((slot, i) => ({...slot, id: String(i), date: DEMO_DATE}))
  .filter(bookable);

const state = { step: 0, service: "", vet: "any", slot: "" };
const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
const selectedSlot = () => slots.find(slot => slot.id === state.slot);
const matching = (vet = state.vet) => slots.filter(slot =>
  slot.service === state.service &&
  (vet === "any" || slot.vet === vet)
);
const range = slot =>
  `${slot.start}–${clock(minutes(slot.start) + services[slot.service].minutes)}`;

function validSelection() {
  const slot = selectedSlot();
  return Boolean(slot && bookable(slot) &&
    slot.service === state.service &&
    (state.vet === "any" || slot.vet === state.vet));
}
function canContinue() {
  if (state.step === 0) return Boolean(state.service);
  if (state.step === 1) return Boolean(state.vet);
  if (state.step === 2) return validSelection();
  if (state.step === 3)
    return validSelection() && !services[state.service].estimate;
  return false;
}

function radio(name, value, checked, title, detail) {
  return `<label class="option">
    <input type="radio" name="${name}" value="${value}"
      ${checked ? "checked" : ""} required>
    <span><strong>${title}</strong><small>${detail}</small></span>
  </label>`;
}

function sync(announce = false) {
  const service = services[state.service];
  const slot = selectedSlot();
  $("sum-service").textContent = state.service || "Not selected";
  $("sum-price").textContent = service
    ? service.price + (service.estimate ? " — exact total required" : "")
    : "Not selected";
  $("sum-vet").textContent = slot ? `Dr. ${slot.vet}` :
    !service ? "Not selected" :
    state.vet === "any" ? "Any available vet — assigned with your time" :
    `Dr. ${state.vet}`;
  $("sum-time").textContent = slot ? `${range(slot)} (clinic-local)` :
    "Not selected";
  $("next").disabled = !canContinue();

  if (announce) {
    $("status").textContent =
      `Summary updated. ${$("sum-service").textContent}. ` +
      `Price: ${$("sum-price").textContent}. ` +
      `Vet: ${$("sum-vet").textContent}. ` +
      `Time: ${$("sum-time").textContent}.`;
  }
}

function render(focus = true) {
  const titles = [
    "Choose a service", "Choose a vet", "Choose a time",
    "Review & confirm", "Demo appointment confirmed"
  ];
  let body = "";

  if (state.step === 0) {
    body = `<p class="muted">Common visits first. Prices are shown before booking.</p>
      <fieldset><legend>Service and price</legend><div class="options">
      ${Object.entries(services).map(([name, service]) =>
        radio("service", name, state.service === name, name,
          `${service.minutes} min · ${service.price}` +
          (service.restricted ? " · Dr. Mary Major only" : ""))
      ).join("")}
      </div></fieldset>
      <p class="muted">Dental cleaning starts at $280, not a final total.
      An exact quote must be supplied and accepted before booking.</p>`;
  }

  if (state.step === 1) {
    const eligible = Object.keys(vets).filter(vet =>
      qualifies(vet, state.service) && vets[vet].includes(DAY)
    );
    const countText = vet => {
      const count = matching(vet).length;
      return `${count} bookable ${count === 1 ? "time" : "times"} in the supplied Thursday data`;
    };
    body = `<p class="muted">“Any” shows all eligible vets together.
      Picking a time assigns the named vet.</p>
      <fieldset><legend>Vet preference</legend><div class="options">
      ${radio("vet", "any", state.vet === "any", "Any available vet",
        countText("any") +
        (services[state.service].restricted ? " · Dr. Mary Major only" : ""))}
      ${eligible.map(vet => radio("vet", vet, state.vet === vet,
        `Dr. ${vet}`, countText(vet))).join("")}
      </div></fieldset>`;
  }

  if (state.step === 2) {
    const available = matching().sort((a, b) => a.start.localeCompare(b.start));
    body = `<p><strong>Thursday, October 15, 2026</strong><br>
      <span class="muted">Demo date · clinic-local time · 24-hour clock</span></p>`;
    body += available.length ?
      `<fieldset><legend>Available appointment times</legend>
      <div class="options times">
      ${available.map(slot => radio("slot", slot.id, state.slot === slot.id,
        range(slot), `Dr. ${slot.vet}`)).join("")}
      </div></fieldset>` :
      `<div class="notice"><strong>No bookable times in the supplied data.</strong>
      <p>Go back to change your vet or service.
      Other dates are not included in this demo. This does not mean
      the clinic is fully booked.</p></div>`;
    body += `<p class="muted">Hours: 09:00–17:00.
      Closed for lunch 12:00–13:00. The full visit must fit within opening hours.</p>`;
  }

  if (state.step === 3) {
    body = `<p>Check the appointment below before confirming.</p>
      <div class="edits" aria-label="Edit appointment">
        <button type="button" data-edit="0">Edit service</button>
        <button type="button" data-edit="1">Edit vet</button>
        <button type="button" data-edit="2">Edit time</button>
      </div>`;
    if (services[state.service].estimate) {
      body += `<p class="notice">Booking is blocked until the clinic supplies
        an exact total for you to accept. “From $280” is not a final price.</p>`;
    }
  }

  if (state.step === 4) {
    body = `<p>This is a prototype confirmation only.
      No appointment was sent to the clinic.</p>`;
  }

  $("screen").innerHTML =
    `<h2 id="step-title" tabindex="-1">${titles[state.step]}</h2>${body}`;

  document.querySelectorAll(".progress li").forEach((item, index) => {
    item.removeAttribute("aria-current");
    if (index === Math.min(state.step, 3))
      item.setAttribute("aria-current", "step");
  });
  $("back").hidden = state.step === 0;
  $("actions").hidden = state.step === 4;
  $("next").textContent = [
    "Continue to vet", "Continue to times", "Review appointment",
    "Confirm demo booking", ""
  ][state.step];
  sync();
  if (focus) $("step-title").focus();
}

$("booking").addEventListener("change", event => {
  const input = event.target;
  if (input.name === "service") {
    state.service = input.value;
    state.vet = "any";
    state.slot = "";
  } else if (input.name === "vet") {
    state.vet = input.value;
    state.slot = "";
  } else if (input.name === "slot") {
    state.slot = input.value;
  }
  // Do not re-render radios: preserve keyboard and screen-reader focus.
  sync(true);
});

$("back").addEventListener("click", () => {
  state.step--;
  render();
});
$("booking").addEventListener("click", event => {
  const edit = event.target.closest("[data-edit]");
  if (!edit) return;
  state.step = Number(edit.dataset.edit);
  render();
});
$("booking").addEventListener("submit", event => {
  event.preventDefault();
  if (!canContinue()) return;
  // Local rule recheck only. Production must atomically revalidate and
  // reserve on the server before displaying a real confirmation.
  state.step++;
  render();
});
render(false);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

## 2. Design rationale

### Four short steps, one persistent summary

Separate steps preserve the requested order and reduce competing choices at 375 px. Wellness and vaccination appear first; **Any available vet** is preselected to remove an unnecessary decision. Native radio groups support touch, keyboard and screen readers.

The summary updates immediately. Changing service resets vet preference and time; changing vet resets time. Editing without changing a selection preserves it. With “Any,” selecting a slot reveals its specific vet before confirmation.

The layout uses flexible widths, wrapping text, 16 px page gutters and no fixed-height panels or sticky overlays. Controls have at least 48 px-high interactive areas; focus is visible, step changes focus the heading, and summary changes are announced.

### “From” pricing

“From $280” remains explicitly a starting price—not a promised total. The supplied data cannot support a no-surprises dental booking. Production needs an exact clinic quote accepted before confirmation; until then, confirmation is blocked. This dataset has no valid dental slot anyway.

### Brand departure

White on `#7FD1AE` has approximately **1.8:1** contrast, below WCAG AA even for large text. Primary buttons retain mint backgrounds but use `#1D2B33` labels, approximately **8:1** contrast. Dark borders also identify button boundaries against white.

Other supplied tokens are retained. This implements key AA requirements, but production still needs keyboard, screen-reader, zoom/reflow and device testing.

## 3. Data problems and handling

| Problem | Handling |
|---|---|
| Richard: exotic check-up, 10:00 | Reject: only Mary is qualified. |
| Mary: dental cleaning, 11:30 | Reject: 90 minutes ends at 13:00 and overlaps lunch. |
| Richard: wellness, 12:30 | Reject: appointment begins during lunch. |
| Mary: wellness, 16:45 | Reject: appointment ends at 17:15, after closing. |
| Remaining valid records | Show **Mary’s exotic check-up, 11:00–11:45**, and **Richard’s wellness exam, 14:00–14:30**, only for matching selections. |
| No vaccination slots; no valid dental slots | Show an honest empty state. Do not manufacture availability from working hours or describe missing records as “fully booked.” |
| Thursday has no date or timezone | Clearly label the illustrative date. Production must return dated timestamps and the clinic’s timezone. |
| Dental has only a minimum price | Require an exact quote before committing; the API must provide the final payable total, including applicable mandatory charges. |
| Vet/service references are names; no slot IDs | Production should use stable vet, service and slot identifiers. Demo IDs are local only. |
| Availability may change after selection | Server must enforce qualifications, schedules, full-duration fit, price and inventory atomically. On conflict, retain choices, explain the issue and offer refreshed times—not a false confirmation. |

Both vets work Thursday; Mary’s Tue/Thu/Sat restriction must also be enforced when other dates are introduced.
